{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"We will solve this by integrating by parts. We know that \n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u(x)v\\,^\\prime(x)dx = u(x)v(x)-\\int u\\,^\\prime(x)v(x)dx\\,$.\n\nWe can rewrite this as\n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u\\ dv = uv-\\int v\\ du\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this problem we will let $~u = \\ln x~$ and $~dv= \\dfrac1{x^3}\\,dx\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Then $~du = \\dfrac1xdx~$ and $~v = -\\dfrac1{2x^2}\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Integration by parts gives\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\int^e_1 \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x^3}dx =-\\dfrac{\\ln x}{2x^2}\\Bigg]_1^e+\\int^e_1\\dfrac1{2x^3}dx$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~=-\\dfrac{\\ln x}{2x^2}-\\dfrac1{4x^2}\\Bigg]^e_1=\\Bigg(-\\dfrac{1}{2e^2}-\\dfrac1{4e^2}\\Bigg)-\\Bigg(0-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\Bigg)$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~=\\dfrac{-3+e^2}{4e^2}$","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"question":{"content":"Evaluate $~~\\displaystyle\\int^e_1\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x^3}\\,dx\\,$.\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{-3+e^2}{4e^2}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1+e^2}{4e^2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{-1+2e^2}{4e^2}$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{-3+2e^2}{4e^2}$","correct":false}],"displayCount":null,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"type":"radio","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
